      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start and definitely not spammy, so i appreciate that. \n\nactually, looking at it now, the automated ranking system just flagged this summary as \"low density.\" it's because it's only seeing 6 actionable items. since the engineers are on different sub-teams, it might actually be more helpful for them if we had a bit more granularity. \n\ncan you take another pass at this? try to expand the list so it's more comprehensive. i still don't want you to do anything stupid like \"1. open computer, 2. look at screen,\" but maybe you can pull out the specific sub-components of the larger tasks so the count is higher. just make sure it's still actually useful for the devs.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
